WEBVTT

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:31.290
Iruma Air Base

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:37.160
Whoa! Look at all the planes!

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.120
Calm down, idiot. They'll laugh at you.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:41.200
Good grief.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.160
I get how Miyako feels though.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.580
It's not every day there's a battle this big.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.950
Everyone's on edge.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:54.370
It's a counteroffensive on
a scale unseen. I'm not surprised.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:57.240
Looks like there's a decent turnout.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:02.080
We can thank the dormant period
and napping Pillars for that.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:07.080
Otherwise, Valkyries from all
around the world couldn't come.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:12.160
Valkyries from all around the world!
I can't wait to see what they're like!

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.700
How carefree.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.830
Miko's such a positive girl.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.200
Hey!

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:21.990
You see her face?!

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.830
Jeez, that wasn't very nice.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:27.330
Lizbet! Leyli!

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.990
Yo! It's been a while, Claudia!

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:03.370
Episode 6:
Fuji Pillar Assault !

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:07.660
We've got Japan's best
and aces from far and wide.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.290
What a sight!

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.830
"Dancing Goddess"                               "Maid from Hell"

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.330
Whew! It's really them!

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:12.830
"Einherjar Monthly"
"Maid from Hell: Nina Kolmakov"
"Dancing Goddess: Lhasa Lurizar"

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.580
The Dancing Goddess and Maid from Hell!

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:19.990
Holy smokes!

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:23.620
I thought I'd only see 'em in <i>Einherjar Monthly</i> !

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:24.790
What's that?

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:26.580
A military magazine.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:30.700
It covers the battles
and talks about Valkyries too!

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:34.990
I heard they might cover
our base in the next edition.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:40.410
Wow, awesome! Do you think
they'll take pictures of us and stuff?

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:44.580
Speaking of which,
they approached me for an article once.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:48.790
I sometimes forget,
but you're S-Class, aren't you?

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.370
It's Europe's top three!

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.450
They're mankind's best!

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.620
That's S-Class for you. Center of attention.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.370
Happens all the time.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:04.290
Do you have a cool nickname, Claudy?
Like those other girls?

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.450
A nickname besides Grim Reaper?

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:08.450
That's not cute enough!

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:11.870
Let's think of one more fitting of Claudy!

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:13.080
Princess!

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.080
Angel!

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.370
Glutton!

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:17.290
Would you morons cut it out?!

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:20.820
What a weird bunch you ended up with.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.410
Unbelievable! What's wrong with you guys?!

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:25.580
They sure are. And I'm proud to have 'em.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.240
What's wrong, Lizbet?

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.490
Nothin'.

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:36.870
She's just pouting 'cuz
you're praising them so openly.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:40.040
Lili! Sheesh!

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:44.700
Here I thought you'd be sad
and depressed in Japan.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.580
But you're loving it here!

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:49.580
That's a good thing. How is Japan?

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:52.290
Let's see... The food is good.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:54.120
That's your number one?

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.450
It's important to me. Huh?

00:04:56.450 --> 00:05:01.950
You guys sure get along, Claudy!
You're like total buddies!

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:04.620
These two and I aren't...

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:09.160
No, you're right. They're great friends.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:16.660
Wh-What's got into you?
What do we even say to that, right?

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:19.990
Oh, please. You're happy. I am too though.

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:23.540
Ahem! Man, you're unbelievable.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:26.910
We've been hurting to fill the hole you left.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:30.080
Yeah. I'm sorry about that, but...

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.410
But?

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:36.790
If we defeat the Primary Pillar,
doesn't that more than make up for it?

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:40.240
Look at you, talking all big.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:43.870
Claudy's right! Let's all do our best!

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:46.080
It's a pleasure to work with you!

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.790
Yeah! It's a pleasure!

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.540
Back at you, Miyako.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:52.080
Miko sure acts like a big shot.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.240
More like a big idiot.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.870
I bet she's got no idea how incredible they are.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:01.330
Even if she did, it wouldn't change a thing.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:06.740
Okay, okay! Sorry to spoil all your fun.

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:08.490
It's time to go.

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.990
Shoot! Move your butt!

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:12.910
Let's talk again later!

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:15.330
Sure! Later!

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:17.580
After you, Helmwige.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:21.080
Yeah, yeah. Get moving.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.950
Helmwige?

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:25.330
I thought you wouldn't make it!

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:27.870
Sorry! We were busy talking!

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:31.410
You guys act like the world revolves around you.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.330
Hey, it's starting!

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.660
Who's that on stage?

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:41.580
Commander of the operation, Major General Okita.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.160
Major General?

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:46.330
I guess you'd call him an air vice-marshal.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:50.160
The commander's explaining the plan himself?

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.700
No, there's plenty of officers for that.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:57.120
He's got a job only a commander can do.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:08.120
Six years.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:12.410
Six years since humanity
first encountered the Pillars.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:15.490
And we have only known defeat.

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:19.330
We lost Europe, fled to Asia...

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:27.290
...and in the skies, we fight a losing war
against the Pillars which continue to destroy us.

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:33.120
"Victory" in battle is something
we have yet to claim.

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:38.950
Nevertheless, we have come together.

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:41.620
And for what purpose?

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:44.160
To win.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:45.660
For what purpose?!

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:49.450
T-To win! To be victorious!

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:51.410
For what purpose?!

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:54.160
To take back what they took from us!

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:55.830
To avenge our comrades!

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:58.040
To regain our dignity!

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:00.540
To not lose sight of who we are!

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:03.490
To face tomorrow together!

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:05.910
That's right! You're all right!

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:07.660
For our friends!

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:09.950
For our families!

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:11.700
For our pride!

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:18.240
We're here because of what
now crowns the majestic Mount Fuji!

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:26.450
To tell that preposterous Pillar
that humanity will not be underestimated!

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:29.200
To take back our country.

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:32.290
To take back our future!

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:36.540
Yeah!

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:47.540
Sakura?!

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:52.660
What a speech.

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:56.490
Believe it or not, it touched my heart.

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:58.700
Odin?

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:03.740
Silence. God Odin is our partner
in this counteroffensive.

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:08.910
He's here to encourage everyone
before the operation begins.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:16.330
Yes, that's right. But a speech
like that will be a tough act to follow.

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:18.450
No thanks.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:24.040
Besides, this should be heard
by more than just the warriors here.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:27.670
No Open    Flames

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:27.670
No Open    Flames

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:27.670
No Open    Flames

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:30.490
Hear this, all who have gathered here!

00:09:30.490 --> 00:09:35.870
I do not intend to question
the reasons for which you fight.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:38.490
But, know this...

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:43.790
My daughters and the warriors
who fight beside them--

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:49.240
this battle of yours
I will personally watch over!

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:52.370
My dear humans...

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:59.450
I, Odin, give you my blessing.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:02.120
You have my protection!

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:07.240
We have Odin's protection!

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:11.370
We have Odin's blessing!

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:25.700
Odin! Odin! Odin!

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:25.700
Tsk!

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:27.870
Sigu...

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:29.540
...ruri!

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:32.370
Sigu...

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:33.450
...ruri!

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:37.490
--We've got lots of work to do!
--Hurry it up!

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:43.040
Whew! Everyone's so pumped up!
I guess that's god power for you!

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:46.290
Yeah. That was something else.

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:51.990
Hmm, but we're under orders to standby.
Kinda makes it hard to unwind.

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:58.410
We'll be in the air in a few hours.
Besides, you don't know how to unwind.

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:01.410
Now that you mention it, you're right!

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:04.620
What about you? Are you nervous?

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:06.620
No, I'm fine.

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:09.790
Yeah? If not, you can say something.

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:11.950
You eat something funny today?

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:13.410
Like black cod?

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:14.450
Zip it!

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:15.660
It was tasty.

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:18.790
Could you guys be nervous for once?!

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:21.240
It's Miko and them!

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:23.040
We're home!

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.580
Welcome back!

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:26.790
We heard Odin's speech.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.830
It went out to the whole base!

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:33.370
That's a god for you!
They take it to the next level!

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:35.620
Is Amatsuka not back yet?

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:37.240
Oh, Big Sis?

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:40.290
She walked off with Commander Satomi.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:43.660
Sounded like a serious conversation.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:47.990
Oh, Sono!

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:53.040
I get where you're coming from.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:56.540
I don't want her to fight either.

00:11:56.540 --> 00:12:00.490
But if she doesn't, aren't the others at risk?

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.790
Just let me handle it.

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:04.870
That's why I'm here.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:08.160
That's why I'm S-Class Helmwige.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:11.660
Former. You used to be.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:17.240
I still hear her cries in my dreams
from when she couldn't fly.

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:19.990
I just want her to be safe.

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:22.290
I know you do.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:28.240
But you'll sabotage her plane again,
even if it breaks her heart?

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:35.080
What... did you just say?

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:39.330
Sonoka...

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:44.410
What does he mean?! Answer me, Big Sister!

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:57.660
Sono! Wait!

00:12:57.660 --> 00:12:59.910
I'm sorry you had to see that.

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:01.950
It's fine, but...

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:04.830
What did you mean by that?

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:07.580
Just like you heard.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:10.200
I didn't let her fly.

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:13.490
That is, the day I was shot down.

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:18.520
2 Years Earlier. Hyakuri Air Base, 2023

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:17.540
Mars 1 is hit!

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:18.790
Amatsuka!

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.790
Big Sister!

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:23.620
It's not... a big deal.

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:28.410
This much... won't keep me down.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:29.620
Can I fly yet?

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:33.870
You're kidding! It's in no shape to fly!
Besides, at this point...

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.830
Mars 2, signal lost!

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:39.870
No...

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:42.410
Jinguuji...

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:46.540
Please...

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:50.660
...let me... fly...!

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:53.660
Sonoka, I...

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:58.620
Mars 1, signal lost.

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:00.540
Big Sister!

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:08.830
No!

00:14:08.830 --> 00:14:12.330
Miraculously, I somehow survived.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:17.370
But, I was too ashamed to face her.

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:22.950
Satomi here continued to look
after her, even out in Tateyama.

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:28.990
I was responsible for losing a Named.
They pushed me away from the front lines.

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:34.660
The rest kind of just happened.
I was hardly being noble.

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:37.950
I see! Helmwige...

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:43.450
Two years ago, I took the place
of a Named that got unregistered.

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:47.950
You and Sakura would've been my juniors.

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:50.290
Can I ask you something?

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:53.580
Why did you sabotage Sonoka's plane?

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:56.200
Because I had a bad feeling.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:59.450
One that made the hair stand up on my neck.

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:02.700
You're kidding. That's your reasoning?

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:05.370
It might seem illogical to you.

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:08.040
But it's different for me.

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:14.120
I know what you mean. Sometimes,
it feels like I can sense danger too.

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:17.450
So now you don't want her to fly again?

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:20.700
Unfortunately, it didn't work out this time.

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:26.240
Dammit! It's not like I can fault
you for being overprotective!

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:28.200
I know.

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:30.990
But we need Sonoka.

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:33.240
Not only us...

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:35.950
...but humanity.

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:38.910
This is why I hate war.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:42.540
All right! Azu, Claudy, let's do this!

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:46.450
We've gotta do good so Sono and Big Sis make up!

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:49.910
You're more concerned with them than humanity?

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:53.660
That's Miyako for you. Count me in.

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:56.620
Woohoo! And Azu?

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:58.660
I'll think about it.

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:01.240
How you feeling, Watarai?

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:02.830
Not so good.

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:08.950
Well, I'm not surprised. Honestly,
I thought you might not come back.

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:12.290
That's what Big...

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:15.240
That's what Amatsuka is hoping I'll do.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:20.240
But I decided I'm gonna prove something--

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:23.740
that I can fight too.

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:32.910
All craft in position!

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:43.700
All planes, commence operation!

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:05.410
Secondaries detected. Class 3.

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:12.040
Type C: Cannon Type.
Four, five, six, seven... and increasing!

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:17.290
Class 3: Newly-formed.
Crush 'em while they're weak.

00:17:17.290 --> 00:17:18.330
Roger!

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:20.620
Take this!

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:22.040
One down!

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:24.370
Behind us! Multiple small Pillars!

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:33.660
Hell yeah, baby! Let's rock!

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:37.410
Don't get too worked up. It's hard to cover you.

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:39.200
Try to keep up!

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:42.830
Secondaries are child's play to 'em!

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:45.490
It's like there's two Claudys!

00:17:45.490 --> 00:17:46.370
Hot damn!

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:48.910
Named are sick!

00:17:57.870 --> 00:18:00.120
Its armor is even thicker?

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:02.580
Leave it to me! I've got this!

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:09.540
Take this!

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:11.700
Whew! Sono's awesome!

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:13.990
She can maneuver like that?!

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:18.160
That's a piece of cake for her.
After all, she's...

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:22.200
She's matching Schwertleite's speed?!
Just who is that?!

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:26.580
I see. So that's the world's
youngest Named candidate.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:30.080
No wonder Satomi keeps her close by.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:36.040
To think we would celebrate
children being good at war...

00:18:36.040 --> 00:18:39.120
There's more where that came from!

00:18:40.290 --> 00:18:42.080
All right! My turn!

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:44.040
Save Hero Cannon for later!

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:45.790
Azu, no fair!

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:48.490
75% of Secondaries destroyed.

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:52.080
Minimal damage to Valkyrie Wing.
Able to proceed.

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:57.700
No heat reaction or infrared
reaction from Fuji Primary Pillar.

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.790
It's still quiet.

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:03.290
Excellent. Send Sveið to the front!

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:10.910
A Lancaster?! Where'd that come from?!

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:14.790
That's a Named from England.
It's Sveið's Hero Wing.

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:17.240
Damn, that's a biggie!

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:18.740
Here it comes!

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:22.620
Ten-ton bomb! Slam dunk in your face!

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:38.330
Huh? Damage confirmed
on Primary Pillar's external wall!

00:19:38.330 --> 00:19:41.910
Looks like we can get through! Orders?!

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:44.620
Excellent.

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:45.830
Proceed!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.620
Roger!

00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:56.120
It seems way bigger on the inside.

00:19:56.120 --> 00:20:00.870
Primary Pillars are only 500 meters in diameter.

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:03.830
Must be one of those "other dimensions."

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:07.240
Be careful. There's no telling what'll happen.

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:10.620
What's that supposed to mean? Hmm?

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:11.910
Huh?

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:18.740
Those are...!

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:22.490
Where in the world did
all those planes come from?

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:26.370
All these people weren't sent off?

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:31.120
It's like a graveyard of people
who were shot down by Pillars.

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:35.700
And not just from Japan.
There's planes from all over.

00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:39.200
Bizarreness aside, this makes me sick!

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:43.950
We'll worry about sending them off later.
Let's finish the fight.

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:45.200
General?

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:50.370
I know. Locate the Vandrande
as quickly as possible.

00:20:50.370 --> 00:20:52.490
The dead are coming.

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:54.870
Hmm? What was that?

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:58.740
There was no early warning!

00:20:58.740 --> 00:21:00.830
Enemies incoming! Spread out!

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:03.950
Rog-- Whoa! Where'd that come from?!

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:06.240
From below! But...

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:17.290
You're shitting me!
How dare you desecrate the dead!

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:18.540
Azu...

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:20.040
Wait!

00:21:21.490 --> 00:21:23.120
That's gotta be it!

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:36.040
A giant?!

00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:39.490
Thor.

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:51.540
You're kidding! Multiple Secondaries
have appeared around Fuji!

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:52.660
Impossible!

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:55.990
Shit! Is something happening outside?!

00:21:58.870 --> 00:22:00.370
Satomi!

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:03.160
That's...!

00:22:03.160 --> 00:22:06.790
No... It can't be...

00:22:06.790 --> 00:22:08.660
Mars 2...

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:12.740
Jinguuji's Hero Wing!

00:22:12.740 --> 00:22:17.080
Who?! Who's doing this?!

00:23:57.990 --> 00:23:59.330
<i>Einherjar Monthly</i> !

00:23:59.330 --> 00:24:01.740
This month, Dancing Goddess and Maid from Hell!

00:24:01.740 --> 00:24:03.830
Featuring interview with Rossweisse!

00:24:03.830 --> 00:24:05.830
Column "Our Dear Valkyries"!

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:07.370
Next month, Japan special!

00:24:07.370 --> 00:24:09.370
Check out the swimsuit pinups!

00:24:09.370 --> 00:24:12.120
We'd love to hear from you!

00:24:10.120 --> 00:24:12.120
Next Time

00:24:10.120 --> 00:24:12.120
Episode 7
Fuji Pillar Retreat !
